<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" version="1.1" creator="mtl_bike tools/build.py" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd"><metadata><name>6-Day Tour (Sunday to Friday)</name><desc>475.5 mi total. For bike computers, prefer the one-file-per-day GPX files in gpx/.</desc></metadata>
  <wpt lat="44.69771" lon="-73.49193"><name>Hotel: Best Western Plus Plattsburgh</name><desc>Mile 72.5. 446 Route 3, Plattsburgh, NY. (518) 561-7750. On Route 3 by I-87 exit 37, about 2 mi west of downtown.</desc><sym>Lodging</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.69935" lon="-73.47864"><name>Bike: Maui North Ski, Bike &amp; Board</name><desc>Mile 71.7, 0.2 mi off route. 316 Cornelia St, Plattsburgh, NY. (518) 563-7245. Full-service shop on the route into town. Listed Mon to Fri 10 to 6, Sat 10 to 5, Sun 12 to 4.</desc><sym>Bike Trail</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.69672" lon="-73.44645"><name>Station: Plattsburgh</name><desc>Mile 70.3, 0.2 mi off route.</desc><sym>Train</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.99315" lon="-73.36424"><name>Lunch: Lakeside Coffee Roasters</name><desc>Mile 28.1. 109 Lake St, Rouses Point, NY. (518) 297-5600. Last US cafe before the border. Paninis, quiche, soups. Listed Tue to Fri 7:30 AM to 2 PM (one source says Fri closes 1:30), Sat and Sun 8 to 2, closed Mon. The Lake Street Cafe &amp; Bakery listed in earlier drafts closed in Oct 2025.</desc><sym>Restaurant</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.50447" lon="-73.56234"><name>Hotel: Hôtel Monville</name><desc>Mile 87.6, 0.4 mi off route. 1041 Rue de Bleury, Montréal, QC. +1 (514) 379-2000. Downtown, about 0.5 mi from Place Jacques-Cartier. Ask about bike storage when booking.</desc><sym>Lodging</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.50020" lon="-73.56848"><name>Hotel: Fairmont The Queen Elizabeth</name><desc>Mile 87.4, 0.7 mi off route. 900 Boul. René-Lévesque O, Montréal, QC. +1 (514) 861-3511. Above Gare Centrale. Unboxed bikes still cannot board Amtrak here.</desc><sym>Lodging</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.35408" lon="-73.29597"><name>Bike: Cycle LM</name><desc>Mile 58.4, 1.3 mi off route. 270 Boul. Saint-Luc, Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, QC. . Bike shop with a repair workshop, about 2.4 mi west of the route. Replaces 'Performance Bégin', which could not be found. Phone not verified: see cyclelm.com.</desc><sym>Bike Trail</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.50583" lon="-73.55314"><name>Bike: Ça Roule Montréal / Montreal on Wheels</name><desc>Mile 87.7. 27 Rue de la Commune E, Montréal, QC. +1 (514) 866-0633. Rental and repair shop at the finish in Old Montreal. October hours listed 10 AM to 5 PM daily.</desc><sym>Bike Trail</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.01030" lon="-73.37086"><name>BORDER: Rouses Point–Lacolle 223</name><desc>Mile 29.4. Open 8 AM to 8 PM daily (both sides). Passport, EDL or NEXUS. No cannabis.</desc><sym>Crossing</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.30959" lon="-73.25229"><name>Food: Bistro La Trinquette</name><desc>Mile 53.1. 290 Rue Champlain, Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, QC. +1 (450) 349-1811. Pub-bistro with a big terrace, not a crêperie. Open late daily; lunch opening time not confirmed.</desc><sym>Restaurant</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.44423" lon="-73.26440"><name>Food: Boulangerie du Vieux-Chambly</name><desc>Mile 65.9, 0.2 mi off route. 2403 Av. Bourgogne, Chambly, QC. +1 (450) 447-9991. Bakery and cafe on the route, about 0.5 mi before Fort Chambly. Sandwiches and pastries. Replaces Fourquet Fourchette, which has closed.</desc><sym>Restaurant</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.99500" lon="-73.37117"><name>Station: Rouses Point</name><desc>Mile 28.3, 0.3 mi off route.</desc><sym>Train</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.52493" lon="-73.52192"><name>Station: Longueuil–Université-de-Sherbrooke</name><desc>Mile 80.9, 0.1 mi off route.</desc><sym>Train</sym></wpt>
  <trk><name>Day 6 (Friday Oct 9): Plattsburgh, NY to Old Montréal, QC</name><desc>87.9 mi (141.5 km), about +600 ft. Routed on OpenStreetMap along the official trails.</desc><trkseg>
